{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1351202-elemental-mastery-technique-help","id":1351202,"title":"Elemental Mastery Technique Help","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-11-26T19:28:06-08:00","id":1351202,"title":"Elemental Mastery Technique Help","content":"So I'm building a test character with the idea of him being a low-powered Nova in the Aeon era. He has Quantum 2 with two points of Transcendence (my rule is that every point of Quantum purchased brings a point of Transcendence but Quantum is automatically bought &quot;tainted.&quot;). I want to set him up as having Elemental Mastery (Time). So far I've got:<br /> <br /> Elemental Mastery (Time) - 2 Power Tags Techniques (2)<br /> <br /> Technique 1: Cloak - 2 Tags: Broadband, Chemical, Sonic, Increased Cost (-2) [The opposite of Reduced Cost(2), each level of Increased Cost raises the cost of using the power by 1 Q]<br /> <br /> Technique 2: Quantum Attack: Entangle (2); Increased Cost (-2)<br /> <br /> Am I doing this right? There was something in the file about how each Technique power in the Power suite had to have Technique attached to it. However, there's also something about how the Techniques can't have more in Power Tags than the base power. The problem is that Elemental Mastery doesn't really have a base power. The whole thing manifests through various Techniques.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2318-johntfs","name":"johntfs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"373"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-27T09:51:35-08:00","id":1351305,"title":"","content":"This was posted at the tail end of the KS by Danielle (one of the Devs)<br /> <br /> 'About the Technique Tag: after reviewing it last night, we decided that we needed to change how you got Power Suites in general to prevent confusion on when you needed the Technique Tag, and also prevent an infinite loop exploit we found from it being a Tag. Now you purchase Power Techniques as a Mega-Edge for a certain power which clearly limits it to your Quantum rating per power, and removes the confusion of if you need to apply the Tag to the new power, etc. We'll be updating the manuscript with the change, but it doesn't change what the Power Suit is, so I'll do an example or two here:'<br /> 'Ex 1. Okay so say you've got an Elemental Mastery over magnetism. Let's rate that at 3 (even though that rating here doesn't matter for Mastery, it does for other powers) with the starting power of Environmental Anima and give it the tags: Range 2. So we have 3 dots in the power and 2 tags. When we add a Power Technique, we choose another power and get it at the same dot rating and with the same number of tags as our Elemental Mastery, so we pick Quantum Attack which is a 3 dots, and get to pick 2 tags, let's go with Range 1 and Stun. Next we want to also fly, so we Technique Flight which is also at 3 dots, and we go ahead and give it the tags Bestow and Impose.'<br /> 'Now, when we activate Elemental Mastery (Environmental Anima) to move stuff with magnetism, we can take a mixed action to toss that item as part of a Quantum Attack, and we can take to the air and fly around, and bring our friends in close range with us. Or maybe we pick up an enemy at close range and collide him with a steel beam as a mixed action.'<br /> 'Ex. 2 You have a Quantum Attack which is a beam of yellow light. Let's rate it at 2 and it automatically gets the Close Tag, we get a free tag from the dot rating so Beam (since that's how we described it) and then we buy an additional Tag of Piercing. We want to add a Technique of Quantum Leech, so when we get it, it give us Quantum Leech at 2 dots and 1 Tag (based on what we purchased, not what the thing gave us originally) and get Vampiric to give us more bang for our buck on that hit. Now we can choose to beam attack you, or leech from you, or do both in conjunction as a mixed action which would trigger our Vampiric Tag.'<br /> 'Okay, so the Technique is no longer a Tag, but a Mega-Edge (will be reflected in the manuscript) but otherwise, your breakdown is correct. BTW, I didn't mention tags given by dots in Elemental Mastery because that power does not give free tags for dot ratings.<br /> <br /> So in our example 1 you'd need Quantum 2 to get 2 dots of the Power Techniques Mega-Edge to get both the powers added to the suite (but 3 dots really to have Elemental Mastery rated at 3).<br /> <br /> And yes, you can always choose to have less dots or tags on a power you add with a Technique if you want. You just can't go over the dots you have on the original power.'","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Raksha are my fae-vorite.<br /> <br /> Reincarnation of magnificentmomo.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1542-morosemorgan","name":"MoroseMorgan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1542_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"778"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-27T10:26:19-08:00","id":1351311,"title":"","content":"So, unlike most Mega-Edges, Power Technique is linked to Quantum instead of a Mega-Attributed. Is it also linked to the power? Like a character has Quantum 5, but only 2 Dots in Elementary Mastery (Time). Can the character buy 5 Techniques (in addition to the base effect), 4 Techniques (the base effect counts as a Technique), 2 Techniques (two dots in the power) or only 1 Technique?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2318-johntfs","name":"johntfs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"373"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-28T20:47:05-08:00","id":1351581,"title":"","content":"The thing is we don't have an official answer on what the actual version for Elemental Mastery technique building is going to look like. Which means its hard to actually answer you on the best or even real way to write them up. <br /> <br /> Honestly, while I get them not giving us a full copy of the book till its closer to release, I do hope they provide us with at least this particular rule set - that way we can actually see how power groups are made.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-28T22:40:14-08:00","id":1351594,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LordHeru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1351202-elemental-mastery-technique-help?p=1351581#post1351581\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The thing is we don't have an official answer on what the actual version for Elemental Mastery technique building is going to look like. Which means its hard to actually answer you on the best or even real way to write them up.<br /> <br /> Honestly, while I get them not giving us a full copy of the book till its closer to release, I do hope they provide us with at least this particular rule set - that way we can actually see how power groups are made.</div> </div> </div> </div>Looking it over, it seems like my first thought is correct. The limiting factor is Quantum but not Dots. With Quantum 2, a character with EM (Time) gets one basic technique and then can buy two Mega-Edge Techniques. No technique can have more dots than the base power. No technique can have more net positive tags than the base power. So, if my base power was Quantum Attack (Aging) bought as Aggr(2), Poison (2); Restricted: Organic only (-2); Increased Cost (-2) that's a net positive Tag of 0. Any technique would either have no tags or have to have any positive tags offset by negative tags. However, &quot;free&quot; tags (due to increased Dots in a power) don't count toward the total. So if one of the techniques was Cloak 2, I could get Broadband (1), Sonic (1) or Chemical (1) for &quot;free&quot; but need to offset the cost if I wanted to begin with the other two, assuming the base power's tag cost was 0.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2318-johntfs","name":"johntfs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"373"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-29T01:56:38-08:00","id":1351615,"title":"","content":"Okay, here's a question. Does Elemental Mastery actually exist? By which I mean, in Mutants &amp; Masterminds 3e, you can get an array of powers by buying a base power and then getting a bunch of alternate techniques for it, and give it a name like &quot;Fire Mastery&quot; or something, but there's no actual Fire Mastery power, it's just a name you gave a power you bought that you also bought a bunch of alternate powers for. And from what I can tell, the Aberrant rules for alternate powers works exactly the same as in Mutants &amp; Masterminds; you can buy a power, then get tags to get a bunch of alternate powers as long as none of those alternate configurations have a higher XP power than the first power.<br /> <br /> Does Elemental Mastery currently do anything different from just buying a power and then buying alternate versions (techniques or whatever they're called)? Like, is there any difference in buying Air Mastery with a base power of Quantum Anima and an alternate power of Quantum Attack, and just buying a Quantum Anima power with an alternate power of Quantum Attack? If not, then it seems like one of those &quot;this is how you do something with this system&quot; examples rather than an actual quantum power. Except with language that's kinda confusing to people who haven't played M&amp;M 3e.<br /> <br /> I'm okay with Elemental Mastery working like that, but I'll admit I wasn't very excited by it. I do understand that going with a 1e approach where you define a bunch of different things like Entropy Control, Gravity Control, etc. would have taken a lot more word count and possibly been clunky, but it was kinda cool to have specific (and sometimes unique) powers for those things instead of just building them with effect-based other powers. But again, I'm okay with it, just not inspired.<br /> <br /> EDIT: And again, I might have just totally, completely misunderstood how the power works and if so, my fault for not understanding it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1711,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1711-zeea","user":"Zeea","date":". 11-29-2019, 04:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1711-zeea","name":"Zeea","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"106"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-29T03:32:13-08:00","id":1351624,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zeea</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1351202-elemental-mastery-technique-help?p=1351615#post1351615\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, here's a question. Does Elemental Mastery actually exist? By which I mean, in Mutants &amp; Masterminds 3e, you can get an array of powers by buying a base power and then getting a bunch of alternate techniques for it, and give it a name like &quot;Fire Mastery&quot; or something, but there's no actual Fire Mastery power, it's just a name you gave a power you bought that you also bought a bunch of alternate powers for. And from what I can tell, the Aberrant rules for alternate powers works exactly the same as in Mutants &amp; Masterminds; you can buy a power, then get tags to get a bunch of alternate powers as long as none of those alternate configurations have a higher XP power than the first power.<br /> <br /> Does Elemental Mastery currently do anything different from just buying a power and then buying alternate versions (techniques or whatever they're called)? Like, is there any difference in buying Air Mastery with a base power of Quantum Anima and an alternate power of Quantum Attack, and just buying a Quantum Anima power with an alternate power of Quantum Attack? If not, then it seems like one of those &quot;this is how you do something with this system&quot; examples rather than an actual quantum power. Except with language that's kinda confusing to people who haven't played M&amp;M 3e.<br /> <br /> I'm okay with Elemental Mastery working like that, but I'll admit I wasn't very excited by it. I do understand that going with a 1e approach where you define a bunch of different things like Entropy Control, Gravity Control, etc. would have taken a lot more word count and possibly been clunky, but it was kinda cool to have specific (and sometimes unique) powers for those things instead of just building them with effect-based other powers. But again, I'm okay with it, just not inspired.<br /> <br /> EDIT: And again, I might have just totally, completely misunderstood how the power works and if so, my fault for not understanding it.</div> </div> </div> </div>As far as I can tell, Elemental Mastery does <i>not</i> exist as its own actual power. Taking the example I'm putting together, I get:<br /> <br /> EM (Time) 2: Base[Quantum Attack 2 (Range 1, Entangle (2), Increased Cost (-2)); Mega Edge Technique EM(Time) Cloak 2 (Broadband 1, Chemical 1, Sonic 1, Increased Cost (-2))<br /> <br /> The real power of Elemental Mastery is to allow a character to have multiple powers for a much lesser cost as long as there's some justification for them being in a theme. The above EM (Time) power costs 48 XP. Buying those components separately would cost 60 XP if the powers and techniques were purchased separately.<br /> <br /> Still the character I'm building has limits others won't have. Let's says the guy has a Quantum of 4 and 4 dots in the power EM (Fire) with the Base being Quantum Attack (Range 1, Incendiary 2). That costs 72 XP. However the player can also buy four more techniques which would also cost 72 xp each for 12 xo each. The disadvantage is that if the power is targeted by Quantum Imprint or Quantum Disruption, all of those power get copied/surpressed. Also, you'll be doing a lot of mixed actions.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2318-johntfs","name":"johntfs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"373"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-29T08:11:18-08:00","id":1351661,"title":"","content":"Elemental Mastery does not exist as a power, just as a symbol of status... It is not a power per se, but a tip of how to create your own powers from the effects we got from other powers.<br /> <br /> I personally would exclude it and create a more complete description of the techniques and all the rules related to it, including the power themes and when you can pick a mega enhancement or mega atribute as a technique.<br /> <br /> One of my players (I have an almost active group for Aberrant now!) is building a Superboy stile tank, he have tactile telekinesis, what makes him mega strong, but showily also give him other options as he evolves in the future. I miss a support for that option.<br /> <br /> Other examples are electromagnetic mastery that don\u2019t allow a possible cyberkinesis, or a time manipulation that don\u2019t allow to be Mega Dexterous (can be fast but not do it with cautious and slowly in hyper speed).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-29T10:33:25-08:00","id":1351681,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>johntfs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1351202-elemental-mastery-technique-help?p=1351624#post1351624\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As far as I can tell, Elemental Mastery does <i>not</i> exist as its own actual power. Taking the example I'm putting together, I get:<br /> <br /> EM (Time) 2: Base[Quantum Attack 2 (Range 1, Entangle (2), Increased Cost (-2)); Mega Edge Technique EM(Time) Cloak 2 (Broadband 1, Chemical 1, Sonic 1, Increased Cost (-2))<br /> <br /> The real power of Elemental Mastery is to allow a character to have multiple powers for a much lesser cost as long as there's some justification for them being in a theme. The above EM (Time) power costs 48 XP. Buying those components separately would cost 60 XP if the powers and techniques were purchased separately.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think there's supposed to be an XP discount? As far as I can tell, you're just supposed to get one power from Elemental Mastery that costs the same XP as Elemental Mastery, and then you can buy alternate powers for 12 XP each just like you can with any other power.<br /> <br /> Like, Elemental Mastery (Fire) 3 would cost 36 XP and give you Quantum Attack 3, then you can spend 12 XP each to get alternate powers (techniques or whatever they call it.)<br /> But Quantum Attack 3 would cost 36 XP and then you can spend 12 XP each to get alternate powers (techniques or whatever.)<br /> <br /> As far as I know, if you add tags to any power, any alternate powers get that many tags as well, whether they're techniques from Elemental Mastery or not?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1711-zeea","name":"Zeea","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"106"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-29T10:41:20-08:00","id":1351685,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1351202-elemental-mastery-technique-help?p=1351661#post1351661\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Elemental Mastery does not exist as a power, just as a symbol of status... It is not a power per se, but a tip of how to create your own powers from the effects we got from other powers.<br /> <br /> I personally would exclude it and create a more complete description of the techniques and all the rules related to it, including the power themes and when you can pick a mega enhancement or mega atribute as a technique.<br /> <br /> One of my players (I have an almost active group for Aberrant now!) is building a Superboy stile tank, he have tactile telekinesis, what makes him mega strong, but showily also give him other options as he evolves in the future. I miss a support for that option.<br /> <br /> Other examples are electromagnetic mastery that don\u2019t allow a possible cyberkinesis, or a time manipulation that don\u2019t allow to be Mega Dexterous (can be fast but not do it with cautious and slowly in hyper speed).</div> </div> </div> </div>You mean, basically having power sets defined where you have a specific path of advancement open (like in 1e), instead of just &quot;you get a power and you can branch it out in any direction as long as it makes sense&quot; with no mechanical limits? You know, I think it'd be cool to make pre-defined power sets like that as an optional alternative to the normal freeform version, with a small XP discount so they're not just flat-out worse than free form. It'd take some work, but I think it could be easy to homebrew. Maybe not as satisfying as an official version, but still could be cool. I might give it a shot sometime.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1711-zeea","name":"Zeea","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"106"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-29T10:49:08-08:00","id":1351687,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>johntfs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1351202-elemental-mastery-technique-help?p=1351311#post1351311\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, unlike most Mega-Edges, Power Technique is linked to Quantum instead of a Mega-Attributed. Is it also linked to the power? Like a character has Quantum 5, but only 2 Dots in Elementary Mastery (Time). Can the character buy 5 Techniques (in addition to the base effect), 4 Techniques (the base effect counts as a Technique), 2 Techniques (two dots in the power) or only 1 Technique?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's my read of it. Also, there are a few MEdges based on Quantum. Durability comes to mind.<br /> <br /> The one thing that wasn't directly answered was if when you buy a power that has free tags as a technique if you get the free tags. The RAW of the original techniques and the proposed change would be no, but that hardly seems intentional. I'd give a techniqued Quantum Attack all of its bonus tags, but if you buy techniques off of QA, they don't get it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Raksha are my fae-vorite.<br /> <br /> Reincarnation of magnificentmomo.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1542-morosemorgan","name":"MoroseMorgan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1542_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"778"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-29T17:11:54-08:00","id":1351744,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zeea</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1351202-elemental-mastery-technique-help?p=1351681#post1351681\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't think there's supposed to be an XP discount? As far as I can tell, you're just supposed to get one power from Elemental Mastery that costs the same XP as Elemental Mastery, and then you can buy alternate powers for 12 XP each just like you can with any other power.<br /> <br /> Like, Elemental Mastery (Fire) 3 would cost 36 XP and give you Quantum Attack 3, then you can spend 12 XP each to get alternate powers (techniques or whatever they call it.)<br /> But Quantum Attack 3 would cost 36 XP and then you can spend 12 XP each to get alternate powers (techniques or whatever.)<br /> <br /> As far as I know, if you add tags to any power, any alternate powers get that many tags as well, whether they're techniques from Elemental Mastery or not?</div> </div> </div> </div>The &quot;discount&quot; in XP comes from buying the powers as part of Elemental Mastery. Buying them as full, separate powers raises the cost to 60. The people who really clean up with this are the ones who have invested in a high Quantum (for more techniques) and also bought their base power high and with good tags. My Time Manipulator saves 12 XP. My second example with Quantum 4 EM (Fire) 4 with three tags in the base power could spend a total of 48 points to get four more 4 dot power that had up to three net positive tags on them. Doing that saves him 240 XP.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2318-johntfs","name":"johntfs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"373"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-29T20:12:19-08:00","id":1351774,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>johntfs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1351202-elemental-mastery-technique-help?p=1351744#post1351744\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The &quot;discount&quot; in XP comes from buying the powers as part of Elemental Mastery. Buying them as full, separate powers raises the cost to 60. The people who really clean up with this are the ones who have invested in a high Quantum (for more techniques) and also bought their base power high and with good tags. My Time Manipulator saves 12 XP. My second example with Quantum 4 EM (Fire) 4 with three tags in the base power could spend a total of 48 points to get four more 4 dot power that had up to three net positive tags on them. Doing that saves him 240 XP.</div> </div> </div> </div>Er, I'm confused. Elemental Mastery just uses the Power Suite rules like any other power with alternate powers, and Quantum rating doesn't affect the number of techniques as far as I can see.<br /> <br /> Okay, so your Elemental Mastery (Time) has 2 dots (24 XP) and one Technique (12 XP), and...okay, actually, I'm not entirely sure what's going on here. I don't really think your power set is rules legit. You should have a Quantum Attack 2 with up to 2 points of tags (because Quantum Attack 2 gives you two free tags), but you only have 1 point. You should have a Cloak 2 with up to 0 points of tags (because you don't get to use free Quantum Attack tags in other powers, as far as I know, just purchased tags), and you have 1 point. I'm guessing you forgot the free tag points from Quantum Attack.<br /> <br /> So, anyway, if you bought Elemental Mastery 2, one tag, and one technique (Cloak 2 plus the one tag you bought already), that's 48 XP.<br /> <br /> But if you bought Quantum Attack 2, one tag, and one technique (Cloak 2 plus the one tag you bought already), that's also 48 XP.<br /> <br /> If you bought Quantum Attack 2 with one tag, and bought Cloak 2 with one tag as a full separate power, that's 72 XP, and you can use them at the same time since they're not part of a power suite together<br /> <br /> I'm not sure where 60 XP comes from?<br /> <br /> EDIT: I mean, as far as I can tell Elemental Mastery (Time) with Quantum Attack as the base power is literally the same as any other power suite with Quantum Attack as the base power.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1711-zeea","name":"Zeea","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"106"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-30T02:12:34-08:00","id":1351814,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zeea</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1351202-elemental-mastery-technique-help?p=1351774#post1351774\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Er, I'm confused. Elemental Mastery just uses the Power Suite rules like any other power with alternate powers, and Quantum rating doesn't affect the number of techniques as far as I can see.</div> </div> </div> </div>It\u2019s a rule for tags as general, no tag can be bought if it costs more than your Quantum. It includes multiple times the same tag, for example, you have Q3, you can buy Ranger (2) but can t buy it a second time, because it will cost 4 total. Technique, as a tag, can\u2019t cost more than quantum, so it\u2019s 1 base power + 1 technique por quatum.<br /> <br /> The idea behind it, as I see, is a powerful Nova can learn new powers easily, while a new year can\u2019t, as long it fit in the theme of the powers. You have Elemental mastery, when you Quantum increases you can learn more ways to use it, spending only 14 XP instead of spending 14 times the number of dots and tags.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":24985,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","user":"Mateus Luz","date":". 11-30-2019, 05:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-30T03:02:48-08:00","id":1351821,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1351202-elemental-mastery-technique-help?p=1351814#post1351814\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It\u2019s a rule for tags as general, no tag can be bought if it costs more than your Quantum. It includes multiple times the same tag, for example, you have Q3, you can buy Ranger (2) but can t buy it a second time, because it will cost 4 total. Technique, as a tag, can\u2019t cost more than quantum, so it\u2019s 1 base power + 1 technique por quatum.<br /> <br /> The idea behind it, as I see, is a powerful Nova can learn new powers easily, while a new year can\u2019t, as long it fit in the theme of the powers. You have Elemental mastery, when you Quantum increases you can learn more ways to use it, spending only 14 XP instead of spending 14 times the number of dots and tags.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, okay, I reread the developer commentary on the Mega-Edge version. So apparently it's going to be just one Mega-Edge called Technique with multiple dots, instead of one single-point Mega-Edge per technique. (The current thing with technique tags has a weird cascade effect and no exact reading of it actually makes sense since it'd basically give you infinite techniques once you bought the tag once under a literal reading, which definitely wasn't the intention.)<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1711-zeea","name":"Zeea","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"106"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}